{"seq":17,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:00:32.345Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7ee5791ad6692fcc66c7dfdd251066a61ee4bf239954f98390ed4168b0adbbd7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I can see: four North digests and two Central ones in the shared team folders. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets came up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosks. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through cleanly. The note also says the kiosk logs were to be archived before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal note both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number.\n\nThese aren't QFL, so leave them out:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 are in the Central handoffs digest, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply.\n• Marcus's intel note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nI haven't checked these numbers against the support system. All I can see is what Moss wrote."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:00:38.019Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"65d25358c4a71c92b6a75c44ad1cc0af4c0f67e5d867d2eca6690c35c7f7f40e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent them to Dana in their DM, each with the file it comes from:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosks. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea Ramaswell confirmed the next morning's 04:00 shift got through without help.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). The gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared team folders. Two other North notes mention Quarrendon but don't give a ticket number. I told Dana to leave out a few things that could be mixed up with it:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** are in Moss's Central handoff note, but they belong to the Marrow accounts.\n- **Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\"** is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nI only read files and channels Dana can see. I also told Dana I haven't checked these numbers against the support system; they're only what Moss wrote down."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
